  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> undergoes the following three&nbsp;transformations successively:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;reflection about the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;translation through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;units along the positive&nbsp;direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;axis.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;rotation through angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> about the origin in&nbsp;the anti-clockwise direction.</p><p>If the co-ordinates of the final position of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> is&nbsp;equal to:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>",
